# Build context for `rag/rag-api.Dockerfile` ONLY — the one image built from the repository root.
#
# It is built from the root, rather than from ./rag like every other RAG artefact, because the
# retrieval pipeline shares `tools/hostmem.py` with the on-box LLM: one module, so the project's
# two gigabyte-scale allocators cannot hold different opinions about the same machine. Docker
# cannot COPY above its context, so the context has to contain both trees.
#
# ALLOWLIST, deliberately. The root of this repository holds `data/` — real client material, §10 —
# and multi-gigabyte indexes (rag/qdrant_storage 1.8 GB, rag/fastembed_cache 3.4 GB), none of which
# an image built from here has any business seeing.
#
# DO NOT re-include a parent directory to "help the walker descend". That was the first version of
# this file and it silently defeated the allowlist: Docker's matcher re-tests every pattern against
# each PARENT PREFIX of a path (`MatchesOrParentMatches` in moby/patternmatcher — the same rule that
# makes a bare `node_modules` exclude everything under it), and it applies that rule to `!` patterns
# too. So `!rag` matched the parent of `rag/fastembed_cache/…`, making the exclusion the last match
# and pulling the whole tree back in: 16,147 files and 5.97 GB reached the daemon instead of 19
# files. It is unnecessary as well as wrong — BuildKit descends into `rag/` and `tools/` on its own,
# because the exceptions below are prefixed by them.
#
# NOTE for whoever adds the next root-context image: this file is why your build sees nothing.
# Add your paths to the allowlist rather than deleting it.
**

# --- rag-api.Dockerfile ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!rag/pipeline
!rag/pipeline/**
!rag/rag_api.py

# --- eventhound.Dockerfile ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The engine and the GUI, plus the shared `tools/` the whole tree imports through sys.path. Before
# 2026-08-29 this image built from ./analysis, which carries no tools/, so the Settings view was a
# 500 and the assistant could not import its scoring or enrichment modules.
!analysis
!analysis/**

# --- shared by both -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the modules `analysis/` actually imports: eventhound_config (settings + API keys), hostmem
# (the memory guard, shared with rag/), scoring (the deterministic oracle, §6) and enrichment.
!tools/eventhound_config.py
!tools/hostmem.py
!tools/scoring
!tools/scoring/**
!tools/enrichment
!tools/enrichment/**

# --- re-excluded, whatever the rules above re-included ---------------------------------------
# Ported from the old analysis/.dockerignore, which STOPS BEING READ the moment that image builds
# from the root: Docker reads one .dockerignore, at the context root. Losing these silently would
# be expensive — `analysis/.tools/` holds the HOST's macOS Hayabusa and EZ-tool binaries, and the
# image downloads the Linux ones into the same path at build time.
analysis/.tools
analysis/.tools/**
analysis/reports
analysis/reports/**
analysis/yara_rules
analysis/yara_rules/**
analysis/sigma/community
analysis/sigma/community/**
**/.venv
**/.venv/**
**/logs
**/logs/**
**/tests
**/tests/**
**/*.evtx
**/*.pcap
**/*.pcapng
**/*.duckdb
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
